{
  "schemaVersion": "capability-actions-v1",
  "$comment": [
    "THE ACTION AXIS. SIX CLASSES, SHARED BY ALL 272 TOOLS.",
    "",
    "`idSegments` is the DERIVATION: which words inside a tool id name this",
    "action. Measured on the real registry, 230 of 272 ids carry one, so most",
    "of the catalogue classifies itself. Segments must be unique across actions",
    "-- tools/lib/factor.js refuses to build a table where one segment is",
    "claimed by two actions, because then it is not a derivation.",
    "",
    "`says` is the everyday vocabulary: what a PERSON types for this action.",
    "These words are shared by every tool in the class, which is the entire",
    "point. The first version of this system copied `read` into the file entry,",
    "the email entry, the calendar entry and the clipboard entry and maintained",
    "four copies. Adding a word here now improves every tool that does that",
    "thing, once.",
    "",
    "`says` MAY overlap between actions -- 'tell' is both read and send, 'start'",
    "is both create and run -- because these are words, not codes, and IDF",
    "settles their weight. Only `idSegments` must be exclusive.",
    "",
    "WHY THE READ/WRITE SPLIT IS FREE NOW. The old lexicon needed a hand-written",
    "split for every capability where reading and writing are different tools,",
    "after 'what is on my calendar today' returned calendar.create above",
    "calendar.list. That split is now a property of the structure."
  ],
