  "$overrideComment": [
    "THE RESIDUAL, AND ONLY THE RESIDUAL.",
    "",
    "An id belongs here only when the segment scan cannot resolve it, or resolves",
    "it WRONGLY. This list was 130 entries; widening idSegments to the general verb",
    "space made 101 of them redundant and they were deleted. What is left is real:",
    "ids with no verb at all (sandbox.artifacts, web.fetch, google.accounts), and",
    "ids whose verb means something else here -- model.complete is a run, not a",
    "state change.",
    "",
    "r_ledger.file is the mirror of that case and the reason it is here rather than",
    "in idSegments: 'file' is a VERB in that one id and a NOUN in every other id",
    "that carries it (host.read_file, host.write_file, browser.file_upload). A",
    "segment entry would classify the nouns too, and the first noun-led id whose",
    "real verb came later -- something.file_list -- would derive as a create and",
    "index as a write tool. One override costs one line; a wrong derivation is",
    "silent. r_ledger.propose IS in idSegments: 'propose' is a verb everywhere.",
    "a_ledger.file and t_ledger.file (the ask and task ledgers, 2026-09-07) are the",
    "same case and sit here for the same reason. a_ledger.decline and p_ledger.decide",
    "are NOT here: 'decline' and 'decide' are verbs everywhere, so they are idSegments.",
    "",
    "The list should SHRINK as idSegments grows. If it is growing, the segment",
    "table is not keeping up with how tools are being named."
  ],
